{"schema": 1, "kind": "method", "maps": 901, "clusters": 16, "central": 5, "method": "Ward's agglomerative linkage over palettes.space.distances — 32 samples of each gradient as the renderer spends it (folded where the map is sequential), converted to Oklab, Euclidean over the resulting 96 numbers — cut at 16 clusters. The distance matrix is rounded to 12 decimals before linkage so the merge order does not depend on the platform's linear algebra, and exact ties merge in index order. Each cluster's `central` names are its medoids: the 5 members with the smallest mean distance to the rest of their own cluster, ties broken by name. Nothing downstream reads this file; it is a reading of the library for a figure, regenerated by `fractal-wallpapers palettes clusters`."}
